      "raw_text": "MAGTUTULOY-TULOY PA ANG ULAN? ☔️\n\nPAGASA issued a thunderstorm advisory late Tuesday night, July 8, following heavy rains that caused flooding in several parts of Metro Manila and nearby provinces.\n\nIn its 11:28 p.m. bulletin, the weather bureau said moderate to heavy rainshowers with lightning and strong winds are expected within the next two hours over Metro Manila, Pampanga, Bulacan, Tarlac, Quezon, Laguna, Rizal, and Nueva Ecija.\n\nMeanwhile, heavy to intense rainfall is currently being experienced in parts of Zambales, Batangas, Cavite, and Bataan, which may persist and affect nearby areas.\n\n📸 PAGASA",
      "cleaned_text": "MAGTUTULOY-TULOY PA ANG ULAN? ☔️ PAGASA issued a thunderstorm advisory late Tuesday night, July 8, following heavy rains that caused flooding in several parts of Metro Manila and nearby provinces. In its 11:28 p.m. bulletin, the weather bureau said moderate to heavy rainshowers with lightning and strong winds are expected within the next two hours over Metro Manila, Pampanga, Bulacan, Tarlac, Quezon, Laguna, Rizal, and Nueva Ecija. Meanwhile, heavy to intense rainfall is currently being experienced in parts of Zambales, Batangas, Cavite, and Bataan, which may persist and affect nearby areas. 📸 PAGASA",
      "english_translation": "MAGTUTULOY-TULOY PA ANG ULAN? ☔️ PAGASA issued a thunderstorm advisory late Tuesday night, July 8, following heavy rains that caused flooding in several parts of Metro Manila and nearby provinces. In its 11:28 p.m. bulletin, the weather bureau said moderate to heavy rainshowers with lightning and strong winds are expected within the next two hours over Metro Manila, Pampanga, Bulacan, Tarlac, Quezon, Laguna, Rizal, and Nueva Ecija. Meanwhile, heavy to intense rainfall is currently being experienced in parts of Zambales, Batangas, Cavite, and Bataan, which may persist and affect nearby areas. 📸 PAGASA",
